  "secciones": [
    {
      "id": "regla",
      "titulo": "The rule",
      "bloques": [
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "**Llevar** and **llevarse** have different meanings:"
        },
        {
          "tipo": "tabla",
          "encabezados": [
            "Verb",
            "Meaning",
            "Example"
          ],
          "filas": [
            [
              "llevar",
              "_to take_ someone or something somewhere",
              "Llevo a los niños a la escuela."
            ],
            [
              "",
              "_to lead to_",
              "Sus problemas lo llevaron a la ruina."
            ],
            [
              "",
              "_to carry, to have with you_",
              "Siempre llevo pañuelos."
            ],
            [
              "",
              "_to wear_",
              "Lleva un sombrero horrible."
            ],
            [
              "",
              "_to contain_ (food)",
              "Esta salsa lleva chile."
            ],
            [
              "llevarse",
              "_to take away, to keep_",
              "Me llevo la azul."
            ],
            [
              "",
              "_to get along_ (bien / mal)",
              "Nos llevamos muy bien."
            ],
            [
              "",
              "_to get_ (a fright, a surprise)",
              "Me llevé un susto."
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "With people as the object of **llevar**, add the personal **a**: **llevo a los niños**."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "**Llevar** + time + gerund means _to have been doing_: see [[7176|llevar + gerund]]."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "Tip: **llevar** moves things around; **llevarse** keeps them, or describes how people get along."
        }
      ]
    },
